hamlib
------------------------------------------
The Hamlib project's purpose is to develop flexible and portable shared
libraries that offer a standardized API to control any radio oriented equipment
through a computer interface.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libhamlib-devel-4.7.2-1bl1
  libhamlib4-4.7.2-1bl1
  liblua5.3-5.3.6-4
  libreadline8-8.3-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libusb1.0-1.0.21-1
  libusb1.0-devel-1.0.21-1
  perl_base-5.44.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1
  python3-3.12.12-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.11-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  liblua-devel-5.3.6-4
  libreadline-devel-8.3-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  libusb1.0-devel-1.0.21-1
  libxml2-devel-2.13.9-2
  lua-5.3.6-4
  make-4.4.1-2
  perl-5.44.0-1
  python3-3.12.12-1
  python3-devel-3.12.12-1
  swig-4.5.1-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/Hamlib/Hamlib/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/Hamlib/Hamlib/archive/refs/tags/4.7.2.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack hamlib-4.7.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./hamlib-4.7.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/hamlib-4.7.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/hamlib-4.7.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libhamlib4-4.7.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libhamlib-devel-4.7.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/lua-hamlib-4.7.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/perl-hamlib-4.7.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/python312-hamlib-4.7.2-X.tar.xz

